According to Vogue, the dress was originally created in 2001 by design duo Michael and Hushi. Its distinctive chequered fabric echoed the keffiyeh, a symbol of Palestinian identity and solidarity.
Cate Blanchett's debated Cannes statement
Australian actor Cate Blanchett also sparked discussion at Cannes in 2024 when she appeared in a custom gown that many interpreted as a subtle visual reference to the Palestinian flag.
Cate wore a black gown with a green panel and a pale pink section at the back. When photographed against the red Cannes carpet, many social media users interpreted the resulting combination of colours as a gesture of solidarity with Palestine.
However, Cate herself did not publicly confirm that the ensemble was intended as a pro-Palestine statement.
What is less ambiguous is the actor's wider public advocacy. As a UNHCR Goodwill Ambassador, she has previously spoken about the humanitarian crisis in Gaza and called for a ceasefire.
Saja Kilani brings tatreez to the Golden Globes
Palestinian-Jordanian-Canadian actor Saja Kilani made one of the most direct recent tributes to Palestinian heritage on the 2026 Golden Globes red carpet.
The Voice of Hind Rajab actor wore a custom black gown by Jordanian designer Reema Dahbour inspired by the traditional Palestinian thobe.
The dress incorporated tatreez embroidery around the neckline while combining traditional references with a contemporary, structured silhouette.
